    lib/merkle.ml
    ❯❱ tools.opengrep.qnxml-plain-store-to-shared-word
          Plain (non-atomic) store to a shared region word. Merkle publishes the root last on update, but with
          no release store and no acquire on the reader side, a cross-process reader can observe the new root
          with stale children (or a torn path). If the tree is ever read while another process updates it, use
          store_rel on the root and load_acq on reads, or document a quiescence requirement.

           39┆ t.s.{!i} <- mix value;
            ⋮┆----------------------------------------
           42┆ t.s.{!i} <- mix2 t.s.{2 * !i} t.s.{(2 * !i) + 1}

    lib/pmap.ml
     ❱ tools.opengrep.qnxml-pmap-copy-log-heap-alloc
          The copy log is an OCaml heap list consed per copied node, and the version window is a heap list
          too. Every Pmap.set therefore allocates on the OCaml heap in steady state — the strongest form of
          the "never allocate" claim does not hold for Pmap. Either scope the claim to
          Ring/Arena/Vclock/Merkle, or move the log into the region.

           63┆ log := i :: !log;

